      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Vivian Corvinarus.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 3, power rating 12 → a level 3 Sorcerer player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 3 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Impostor Heir</strong> — Self-Interested / Shadow Estate (Infiltrator, not legitimate heir)</p><p>Status: Deceased — killed by Markop during interrogation aftermath, body burned</p><p>Vivian Corvinarus was not a Corvinarus. Was not female. Was not whatever the dinner guests assumed. Vivian was an impostor who arrived at the Shadow Estate disguised as 'Vivinessa'—a thrall to the manor—and worked their way close to the heirs through deception, patience, and a wig. Their goal was sole inheritance: kill Orangus Cornelius, kill Kyrn Corvinarus, eliminate all other succession claimants, and become the sole ruler of an isolated dimensional pocket. They wielded death magic that BYPASSED the Shadowfell's suppression—a crimson disintegration beam that nearly killed Markop and required divine intervention to survive. They had been 'blighting' manor residents, including the Mazebounds in the hedge grove. They were defeated by Markop and Bowser, captured, interrogated, and killed. Waluigi finds Vivian fascinating in the way a poisonous insect is fascinating—beautiful adaptation, terrible purpose, best observed from a distance. Preferably after someone else has dealt with it. WAH.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Crimson Disintegration Beam</strong> — “They wielded death magic that BYPASSED the Shadowfell's suppression—a crimson disintegration beam that nearly killed Markop and required divine intervention to survive.”</li><li><strong>Impostor</strong> — “Vivian was an impostor who arrived at the Shadow Estate disguised as 'Vivinessa'—a thrall to the manor—and worked their way close to the heirs through deception, patience, and a wig.”</li><li><strong>Components Destroyed</strong> — “Vivian's spell components were subsequently destroyed, preventing a repeat, but the existence of Shadowfell-compatible death magic raises alarming questions about what other weapons might function in suppressed”</li><li><strong>Shadowfell-Compatible Casting</strong> — “They wielded death magic that BYPASSED the Shadowfell's suppression—a crimson disintegration beam that nearly killed Markop and required divine intervention to survive.”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/vivian_corvinarus</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/vivian_corvinarus</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
